00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.370 align:start position:0%
 
have you ever wondered why you're tired  all the time or more likely have you  ever started any training program and  just been far too tired to work out when  the time comes and this extends to other  areas of your life as well maybe you  don't have the energy to do the dishes  at night maybe you wanted to start a new  business or learn a new skill and you  just don't have enough energy to do that  either you just come home and you want  to crash out on the sofa and play Sonic  the Hedgehog over and over again because  it's the best game in the world I'm not  talking about myself here I'm talking  about someone I know I can totally  relate to this day I'm a new parent so  I'm tired all the time I don't know if  I've mentioned that before on this  channel any like maybe a million times  every single opportunity I get point is  lots of us are tired all the time  there are countless different programs  supplements diets and fads out there  that claim to help the only issue is  that none of them really work and even  if they do the change is normally  extremely minor why I'm about to tell  you might seem really obvious to you or  if you're anything like me it might come  as a bit of a revelation when you  realize it for the first time and that  is the single thing that causes most of  us to feel tired is stress and also  doing too much we look at all these  different possible explanations maybe I  need to improve my sleep maybe I need to  take this special supplement maybe I'm  not exercising enough maybe I'm  exercising too much when actually  they're probably just doing too much  stuff and we're too stressed and so we  have no energy to do anything else that  we actually want to do  we're overworked we've burned out the  problem is we slave away at work we've  got a long commute there and back we try  and do all these chores when we come  home we've got social commitments we've  got debt all these other things we're  trying to cram all that in and then on  top of that we're trying to work out as  well and then we wonder why we don't  have energy for it the thing is you need  that recharge time it's not something in  just opt to skip out on you need to  refuel the tank too much exercise too  much activity that won't leave you  mentally exhausted you'll still be able  to come home and read a big book or  start a new project and at the same time  you can also adapt to that kind of  activity emotional tiredness though and  stress that's a whole different kettle  of fish when you spend all day arguing  with people on the phone or being told  what to do or biting your tongue that's  proper exhaustion when you get  home you just won't have the energy or  the inclination to train earthly  whatever else it is that you want to do  from a biological perspective being in a  state of chronic stress means that  you're constantly producing cortisol and  adrenaline you're spending all your time  in a catabolic state burning through  your fuel reserves burning through your  tissue causing a buildup of adenosine  and other byproducts in your brain and  throughout your body eventually get to  the point of adrenal fatigue where your  adrenal glands are just like I'm done  I've got no more adrenaline at that  point you're exhausted of course you're  not gonna be training or starting  anything significant new this is the  point of burnout effectively it's the  same thing as overtraining or  overreaching it's even be referred to as  twenty-first-century syndrome because  it's so prevalent today so if you want  to make a change to your fitness or your  self-development don't start by trying  to add something new start by trying to  take something away you can't just keep  adding more and more commitments and  expect your body and your brain to just  keep up if you want to start a new  training program look at other things  that can cut out look at ways that you  can make your work less stressful maybe  you can remove your commute somehow by  doing a job share or bike using flexi  time or working from home maybe you talk  to your manager because you've got too  much on your plate  maybe you remove some of your social  commitments or your after school  curriculum maybe you hire a cleaner or a  chef or you just find some way to cut  back on all the stuff you're doing so  that you've then got a slot for the new  training program if you're really  committed to getting into shape and  making that kind of change then you need  to cut back on something some people  will say well I can't work less because  my work is so important and I have a  family to support and things well that  might be true and very commendable but  remember that your fitness and your  health are super important as well as  are your happiness and actually maybe  you've got your priorities a bit wrong  if you're working so hard  you've got no energy to do the other  things you want to do in the evening  finally when training or when starting a  new project make sure it's something  you're really excited about because as  we've seen energy comes a lot of the  time from emotion if you're really  pumped for something really psyched  you'll produce hormones but help to  override tiredness so find a way to  train that you enjoy whether that means  starting martial arts or doing a sport  or doing bodyweight training or lifting  heavy weights  remove the bits you're not looking  forward to like the commute to the gym  perhaps or maybe find a training buddy  who you look forward to training with or  treat yourself to a great meal  afterwards whatever the case you should  be replacing something that's draining  with something you can't wait to do the  result is he'll have more energy will  likely stick to your programs and you'll  create more positive change you can then  build off of in the future first just a  little quick tip I hope you found it  useful and interesting if you did then  please leave a like and share around  comment down below and let me know if  this applies to you and stay tuned  because I've got lots more content like  this on the way on fitness brain  training bodybuilding all that cool  stuff if that sounds good  then thanks ton for watching and bye for  now

